      "narrative": "Mara's eyebrow lifts at your question \u2014 a flicker of interest cutting through her guarded stillness.\n\n\"That's a specific question.\" She pulls her cup back and takes a sip, letting the silence stretch. \"The lock on the Ash Gate was maintained by one man, for as long as anyone can remember. Toran Vex. Lockwright.\" She gestures with her chin toward the far corner of the tavern. \"He's sitting over there, ink-stained and nervous as a sparrow in a cat house. He was the one who filed the lock \u2014 sealed it for good, on the council's order.\"\n\nShe watches you, gauging. \"He hasn't talked about it since. Not to me, not to anyone. But he's been drinking here every morning for three days, staring at the same spot on the wall.\"\n\n*Toran Vex* \u2014 a clerk with ink-stained cuffs, hunched over a small table near the shuttered window. He's not looking at you. He's not looking at anything. His hands are wrapped around an untouched cup, and his thumb works a nervous rhythm against the ceramic.\n\nMara lowers her voice. \"If you want to know what happened at that Gate before it was sealed... he's the one who turned the key.\"\n\nShe meets your eyes. \"Good luck. He doesn't trust easy.\""
    },
