      "narrative": "Mara's fingers tighten around her cup as you press her. She holds your gaze for a long moment, weighing something \u2014 trust, maybe, or the cost of speaking plainly.\n\n\"Old Bram,\" she says finally. The name lands flat and heavy. \"He ran the ferry through the Gate. Had done it for longer than anyone in this town has been alive. He'd take people through, bring them back, collect his coin. No questions asked.\"\n\nShe glances toward the shuttered window, toward the direction of the Gate itself.\n\n\"Three nights ago, someone found him at the archway. Throat cut. The lock had been filed clean through \u2014 Toran's work, by council order \u2014 but that happened *after* Bram was already dead. The order came down the same night.\"\n\nShe looks back at you. \"That's all I know for certain. The rest is rumor, and I don't trade in rumor.\""
    },
