      "narrative": "The rain hisses against the churned mud as you step into the field. Your voice cuts across the empty space \u2014 \"Old Bram!\" \u2014 and the name hangs in the damp air, swallowed slowly by the grey morning.\n\nNo answer comes. The treeline beyond the Gate offers nothing. The wind shifts, carrying the smell of wet earth and cold stone.\n\nThe courier near the arch turns at your call. Their hood shifts, revealing a sharp-jawed face, rain beading on unshaven stubble. They watch you for a long moment, then speak \u2014 voice rough, carried by the wet air.\n\n\"You're a few days late. Bram's not answering anyone.\"\n\nThey step closer, boots squelching in the mud. A courier's badge glints dully on their cloak \u2014 a silver quill pin.\n\n\"Sable Quill.\" They offer the name flatly, a habit of introduction rather than warmth. \"I was supposed to deliver a message to him. Found him here three nights ago instead.\" A pause. \"You knew him?\""
