      "narrative": "You crouch beneath the arch, rain trickling down your collar as your eyes sweep the churned mud. Your fingers brush the wet ground, turning over pebbles, scanning for anything out of place \u2014 a scuff mark, a hidden cache, a disturbed patch of earth that might conceal something.\n\nBut there's nothing. Just scattered pebbles, boot-churned mud, and the dark stains near the base of the pillar. Whatever story this ground holds, it's not giving it up to a casual glance.\n\nSable Quill watches you straighten, arms crossed. \"Looking for something specific, or just getting your hands dirty?\" Their tone is dry, but their eyes are sharp \u2014 tracking your movements, your reactions."
